{
  "text": "On the authority of Abu Yala, Shaddad ibn Aus, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may the blessings and peace of Allah be upon him, said, Verily, Allah has prescribed proficiency in all things. Thus, if you kill, kill well, and if you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each one of you sharpen his blade, and let him spare suffering to animal he slaughters. It was related by Muslim.",
